5.3 Anemoi update and sustainability
Summary
This paper provides an update on Anemoi, the European-anchored, openly
developed software infrastructure for data-driven weather forecasting, its
governance, development and future direction. Anemoi is co-developed by ECMWF
and national meteorological services across Europe, which contribute jointly to its
codebase, testing, implementation and evolution. It has rapidly evolved from an
emerging framework into an increasing mature and robust infrastructure
supporting research, pre-operational and operational activities across ECMWF and
its Member and Cooperating States.
Anemoi’s development is coordinated within the European meteorological
community with technical governance provided through the Anemoi Technical
Subgroup (ATS) established within EUMETNET’s E-AI programme, while the
broader strategic direction and long-term sustainability of Anemoi continue to be
shaped jointly by ECMWF and the participating national meteorological services.
This collaborative approach is intended to ensure that Anemoi develops as a shared
European capability, aligned with the evolving needs and priorities of the
community, while remaining open to wider international use and contribution.
Major developments over the past year include substantial improvements in
computational efficiency especially for high-resolution training and inference, an
expanded testing framework spanning a hierarchy of tests, and increased flexibility
to support tasks such as temporal and spatial downscaling, multi-dataset training,
an ensemble of probabilistic techniques and the incorporation of observations.
The paper also reviews progress in Anemoi governance through ATS, identifies
emerging needs for higher-level strategic coordination and sustainability planning,
and summarises findings from the first Anemoi user and developer survey. It also
identifies questions that the evolving governance arrangements will need to clarify,
including responsibilities for strategic priorities, operational release policy,
technical stewardship and long-term resourcing.
Looking ahead, the paper highlights the importance of balancing agility with
operational resilience as Anemoi moves towards version 1 release and continues to
integrate advances from the wider machine-learning community.
